.venv/
__pycache__/
backend/.env
.DS_Store

# Generated by the Water Agent's reference matcher / citizen reports
backend/data/water_dataset_index.npz
backend/data/reports/

# YOLO weights — 6 MB+ binaries, fetched on demand (see backend/.env.example)
backend/models/*.pt

# --- Datasets: excluded from version control -------------------------------------------------
# Two reasons, either of which is sufficient.
#
# SIZE. These total ~11 GB. GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB and a repo this size would be
# unusable to clone. Datasets belong with their publishers, not in application history.
#
# REDISTRIBUTION RIGHTS. Committing a dataset to a public repository is redistributing it.
# IWHR is Apache 2.0 and TUD-GV is CC BY 4.0, so both would need their attribution carried;
# FloW-Img's rights are UNRESOLVED (see docs/DATASET_PROVENANCE.md, blocker B3) and it must not
# be redistributed at all. Provenance, DOIs and licences are documented instead.
datasets/
water_datasets/
garbage_Dataset/
TACO-master/

# Trained weights and training artefacts. Reproducible from the documented scripts and the
# audited split manifests; the reports that justify them are kept (see below).
runs/**/*.pt
runs/**/*.npy
runs/**/*.npz
runs/water/tudgv_yolo/
runs/**/weights/

# Large local demo images kept out of history; the docs name which ones the demo uses.
image*.png
*.jpeg

# Training/evaluation IMAGE artefacts. The reports, metrics and manifests that these illustrate
# are kept (runs/**/*.md, *.json, *.csv) — those are the evidence. The renderings are up to
# 31 MB each and are regenerable from the scripts that produced them.
runs/**/*.png
runs/**/*.jpg
runs/**/*.jpeg
yolov8n.pt
